# Normalize line endings to LF in every checkout. The repo is authored with
# LF and nothing in it is currently CRLF, but Git for Windows defaults to
# `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this a Windows contributor's very first
# clone rewrites every text file and their first commit is an unreviewable
# whole-tree diff. It also keeps CRLF out of files that break on a trailing
# CR — notably the shebang line of the `.mjs` build scripts under scripts/,
# which esbuild and vitest reject as "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected
# token". This repo builds and tests on Windows in CI, so that path is real.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are only meaningful with CRLF. None exist today; the
# rule is here so adding one later doesn't silently produce a broken script.
# PowerShell is fine with LF and is covered by the blanket rule above.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets — never normalize or diff as text. Covers the packaging
# icons, fonts, and screenshots under apps/desktop/build/, docs/assets/, and
# design/uploads/, plus formats a desktop app tends to acquire later.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.mp3   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.mov   binary
*.node  binary

# design/assets/logo-pwrgit.svg is our own hand-editable artwork, so SVG is
# deliberately left as text. Vendor brand-kit SVGs, if any are ever vendored
# in, should be marked binary at that time so refreshes don't diff as XML.
